{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, אָחֳרָן","hw":"אָחֳרָן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אָחֳרָן</span></big>  <strong>adj.m.</strong> another <strong>(</strong>Egyptian Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">אחרן</span> S-C<sup>D 11 +</sup>; Nab.Palm. id. (Lzb <sup>212</sup>); 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">אוּחְרַן</span>; cf.Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐ݈ܚܪܺܝܢ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—<a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:11\" href=\"/Daniel.2.11\">Dn 2:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:44\" href=\"/Daniel.2.44\">44</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:29\" href=\"/Daniel.3.29\">3:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:5\" href=\"/Daniel.4.5\">4:5</a> Kt <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:17\" href=\"/Daniel.5.17\">5:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:24\" href=\"/Daniel.7.24\">7:24</a>. The <strong>f.</strong> in use is <span dir=\"rtl\">אָחֳרִי</span> <strong>(</strong>Egyptian Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">אחרה</span>, RÉS <sup>246</sup>; 𝔗 Talm. <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹחְרִי</span> (D<sup>§ 20. 5</sup>); cf.K<sup>§ 61. 5</sup> M<sup>§ 87 d</sup> Nö<sup> Beitr. 51</sup><strong>)</strong>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:39\" href=\"/Daniel.2.39\">Dn 2:39</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מַלְכוּ א׳</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:39\" href=\"/Daniel.2.39\">39</a> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:5\" href=\"/Daniel.7.5\">7:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:6\" href=\"/Daniel.7.6\">6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:8\" href=\"/Daniel.7.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:20\" href=\"/Daniel.7.20\">20</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנִין","prev":"BDB Aramaic, אַחֲרִית"}